A||N||13||WhiteFieroBlur||Tinting fiero scratched windows||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||12-13-2001||10:49 PM||||I have the usual scratch on my windows that all fieros get. I was wondering if I can change out for a new pair of dew wipes and tint it dark would the scratches show up?||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||12-13-2001||11:32 PM||||I think you will find the scratches stand out even more once you tint the windows. I made this mistake a few years back after I installed new dew wipes...<P>On another note, don't you find it awkward looking when guys tint their rear window and quarter windows, but leave the side windows untinted?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||842m8||12-14-2001||12:38 AM||||I've got another question.... I have my back window tinted it was like that when I bought it but it has a few small peels in it, is it possible to have it removed and redone?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.fortunecity.com/fiero2nv//sitebuildercontent/sitebuilderpictures/girlracer.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-14-2001||07:48 AM||||Yes you can peel it off and redo, but its a real PITA.<P>Some people tint just the rear window so people behind arent staring down their neck. And most places its illegal to tint driver and passenger windows. Lisa got ticketed twice.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||12-14-2001||08:30 AM||||Here you can tint them but it has to be below a certain percentage.  And you have to pay $10 more at inspection time for them to shine a light through it. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||JD86GT350||12-14-2001||07:57 PM||||The side windows in my '84 were scratched pretty good at the felt pad, I put in the new dew wipes and tinted the windows pretty dark (illegal in MI btw) and its just as visible to me on the inside, and upon close inspection, but the car looks much better in my opinion.  No tickets yet, but I don't drive that one much anymore.  I'm planning to go dark on the side windows of the '86 as well.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cyberkhat||12-15-2001||08:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JD86GT350:<BR><B> tinted the windows pretty dark (illegal in MI btw)  No tickets yet, but I don't drive that one much anymore.  I'm planning to go dark on the side windows of the '86 as well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Correct me if I'm wrong but it is NOT illegal in MI to tint your windows as long as they are not darker than a certain amount.What amount I'm not sure...<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000007||Mark Matthews||12-15-2001||09:36 AM||||Here in Vegas it's a certain percentage as well.  However, they don't pull you over for it if it's above it.  I have 10% in front and 5% in back on my old BMW.  Cops always roll by, and mainly just look at the old car!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I guess they figure that out here, you really need it for the heat.<P>One thing to add tho.  If you just want it for UV protection, there is a completely clear 5% out on the market.  I have yet to for doing it at home, but I've seen it at a local tiniting shop.  I may do that on the Fiero, vision is limited anyways.<P>Anybody tint the T-tops?<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||12-15-2001||09:45 AM||||I always tint the back windows of my Fieros so that when a truck or large car is behind me it doesn't blind me with it's headlights.<P>Yes, the scratches will look worse with tint.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula||12-15-2001||10:50 AM||||a scratch looks better then the people who try tinting themselves and have a million bubbles and air pockects imo||||reg||1
Z||000010||JD86GT350||12-15-2001||02:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cyberkhat:<BR><B> Correct me if I'm wrong but it is NOT illegal in MI to tint your windows as long as they are not darker than a certain amount.What amount I'm not sure...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>shrug, I'm new to Michigan, but I've been told by the state police that window tint is illegal.  I know numerous people who have been hassled about it, although they haven't bothered me and my 5% in my work truck.  What they <B>will</B> allow is a tinted strip like 4" across the top of the front side windows (which of course looks lame).||||reg||1
Z||000011||btoth||12-15-2001||02:30 PM||||We have the certain % rule here too, but it seems that the cops will harass you even if it's within the legal limit.<P>I was under the impression that Michigan had more lenient tinting laws.<P>Oh, and as far a scratches... I have them too, I've heard of something called Zaino bros., or something similar?  Any info on that?<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 12-15-2001).]||||reg||1
